{
  "info": {
    "name": "HireMeBot - Recruiter workspace APIs (Cognito access token)",
    "description": "The four recruiter-workspace APIs, authenticated with the Cognito ACCESS token (no recruiter id is ever sent):\n  GET  /api/v1/recruiter/students\n  POST /api/v1/recruiter/applications\n  POST /api/v1/documents/upload-url\n  POST /api/v1/documents/register\n\nEnvironment variables\n  BASE_URL                         http://127.0.0.1:3000 for sam local, or the deployed API URL\n  COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN             SECRET. An access token of an APPROVED recruiter (current value only; never commit or share it)\nOptional (requests that need them are skipped when empty)\n  COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN_PENDING     SECRET. Token of a recruiter still PENDING approval\n  COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN_STUDENT     SECRET. Token of a Google account registered as a student\n  STUDENT_ID                       a student assigned to the approved recruiter\n  OTHER_STUDENT_ID                 a student assigned to a DIFFERENT recruiter\n  RESUME_OBJECT_ID                 a resume object (object_store_entries.object_id) of STUDENT_ID\n\nHow to get a token: sign in to the portal with Continue with Google, then in the browser console run\n  (await fetchAuthSession()).tokens.accessToken.toString()\nand paste the result straight into the variable's current value. It expires after 60 minutes.\n\nExpected results: 200/201 for the approved recruiter on their own students; 401 for no/invalid token; 403 for a pending,\nsuspended, deleted, student or manager account and for another recruiter's student. Deployed, API Gateway answers a missing\nor invalid token with {\"message\":\"Unauthorized\"} before the Lambda, so those tests accept both bodies. See docs/API.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('JSON error envelope on failures', () => {",
          "  if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "    const json = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(json.success === false || json.message !== undefined).to.eql(true);",
          "  }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. GET recruiter/students",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Approved recruiter: own assigned students (200)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/recruiter/students",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "No recruiter id is sent: the acting recruiter is resolved from the token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "(() => {",
                  "  pm.test('200 with only the documented fields', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(json.data.recruiterId).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.data.totalStudents).to.eql(json.data.students.length);",
                  "    json.data.students.forEach(s => pm.expect(Object.keys(s).sort()).to.eql(",
                  "      ['assignedAt', 'email', 'firstName', 'fullName', 'lastName', 'studentId']));",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('actingRecruiterId', String(json.data.recruiterId));",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.test('No server internals, credentials or tokens in the body', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.text();",
                  "    ['jdbc:', 'SQLException', 'at org.hmb', 'password', 'eyJ'].forEach(s => pm.expect(body).to.not.include(s));",
                  "  });",
                  "})();"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Same token + X-Dev-Recruiter-Id and ?recruiterId for someone else: the token wins (200, same recruiter)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Dev-Recruiter-Id",
                "value": "1"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/recruiter/students?recruiterId=1&userId=1",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{COGNITO_ACCESS_TOKEN}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run request 1 first (it records the acting recruiter id)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "(() => {",
                  "  pm.test('The dev header and query parameter have no effect when a token is present', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    const acting = pm.collectionVariables.get('actingRecruiterId');",
                  "    if (acting) pm.expect(String(pm.response.json().data.recruiterId)).to.eql(acting);",
                  "    pm.expect(String(pm.response.json().data.recruiterId)).to.not.eql('1');",
                  "  });",
                  "})();"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Dev header ALONE, no token (deployed: 401; local sam with the flag: 200)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Dev-Recruiter-Id",
                "value": "1000000004"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/recruiter/students",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "(() => {",
                  "  pm.test('Deployed ignores the header (401); only a local sam run with the flag accepts it', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 400, 401, 403]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "    if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 400) {",
                  "      pm.expect(pm.variables.get('BASE_URL')).to.match(/^http:\\/\\/(127\\.0\\.0\\.1|localhost)/);",
                  "    }",
                  "  });",
                  "})();"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
